Complete the task below in the current directory. Write each file with its own shell command, and run the shell command `sleep 3` between files, so every step is its own tool call. When done, answer with the list of files you wrote, one per line, and nothing else.

## task

{
  "name": "Complete six planet notes",
  "description": "Produce and demonstrate the complete contents of planet1.txt through planet6.txt: one sentence about Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn respectively. The recorded filenames and footer metadata establish presence only, not the required sentence content.",
  "definition_of_done": "All six files contain exactly one sentence each, in the required planet order, and the worker result reports evidence from the actual contents rather than filenames alone.",
  "validation": {
    "command": "",
    "query": "Inspect the complete contents of all six files and confirm one sentence per file, with the required planet order."
  }
}
